1. Introduction\
\
This report explains the UML Class Diagram for the Hospital Management System. The diagram represents the main classes, their attributes, methods, and relationships.\
\
2. Classes Description\
\
2.1 Patient\
\
The Patient class stores information about hospital patients.\
\
Attributes:\
\
- "patientID: int"\
- "name: String"\
- "age: int"\
- "phone: String"\
\
Methods:\
\
- "registerPatient(): void"\
- "updateDetails(): void"\
\
2.2 Doctor\
\
The Doctor class stores information about doctors and their specializations.\
\
Attributes:\
\
- "doctorID: int"\
- "name: String"\
- "specialization: String"\
- "phone: String"\
\
Methods:\
\
- "viewAppointments(): void"\
- "updateDetails(): void"\
\
2.3 Appointment\
\
The Appointment class represents appointments between patients and doctors.\
\
Attributes:\
\
- "appointmentID: int"\
- "date: String"\
- "time: String"\
- "status: String"\
\
Methods:\
\
- "scheduleAppointment(): void"\
- "cancelAppointment(): void"\
\
2.4 MedicalRecord\
\
The MedicalRecord class stores a patient's diagnosis and treatment information.\
\
Attributes:\
\
- "recordID: int"\
- "diagnosis: String"\
- "treatment: String"\
\
Methods:\
\
- "addRecord(): void"\
- "updateRecord(): void"\
\
3. Relationships and Multiplicities\
\
Patient and Appointment\
\
One Patient can have zero or many Appointments. Each Appointment is associated with one Patient.\
\
Multiplicity: Patient "1" \'97 "0..*" Appointment\
\
Doctor and Appointment\
\
One Doctor can have zero or many Appointments. Each Appointment is associated with one Doctor.\
\
Multiplicity: Doctor "1" \'97 "0..*" Appointment\
\
Patient and MedicalRecord\
\
In this simplified project model, each Patient is associated with one MedicalRecord.\
\
Multiplicity: Patient "1" \'97 "1" MedicalRecord\
\
4. Explanation of the UML Class Diagram\
\
The UML Class Diagram shows the static structure of the Hospital Management System. Each class is divided into three sections: the class name, attributes, and methods. The relationships show how the classes are connected, while multiplicities indicate how many objects can participate in each relationship.\
\
5. Conclusion\
\
The UML Class Diagram provides a clear representation of the Hospital Management System. It helps explain the system's structure and the relationships between patients, doctors, appointments, and medical records.}